    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Yes, conditionally. The hERG IC50/Cmax margin is approximately:\n\n`30 \u00b5M / 0.05 \u00b5M = 600-fold`\n\nThat is reassuring for hERG-mediated risk, assuming both values are comparable and the free Cmax captures the true peak exposure. It is not, by itself, a complete cardiac safety margin.\n\n**Next testing:**\n1. Confirm hERG concentration-response in an orthogonal, physiologically relevant patch-clamp assay, including measured free concentrations and relevant metabolites.\n2. Run cardiovascular telemetry with toxicokinetic exposure coverage, assessing QT/QTc, heart rate, blood pressure, and arrhythmias.\n3. If needed, add Nav1.5/Cav1.2 profiling to identify non-hERG cardiac liabilities.\n\nI would prioritise Compound A for the next study unless other data show high accumulation, active metabolites, or exposure substantially above the stated free Cmax. The decision would change if the confirmatory assay showed materially greater potency or telemetry showed QT prolongation at clinically relevant unbound exposure.",
